From: Nikita Popov <nikita.ppv@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2020 10:43:58 +0200
Subject: Fix -Wimplicit-function-declaration in configure

As this is an error with xcode 12, see bug #80171.

PHP 7.0 never got this change (PHP 7.3.24). dpkg 1.22 and newer build
with -Werror=implicit-function-declaration, so the test programs that
call memset(), strcmp(), exit() or unlink() without a declaration do not
compile and configure takes that for the answer "no": PHP is built
without getaddrinfo() (names are resolved with gethostbyname(), which
knows neither IPv6 addresses nor IPv6 address literals), without pread()
and pwrite(), with its own crypt() instead of the one of the system and
with the workarounds for a broken sprintf() and for stdio that needs a
flush between reading and writing.

(cherry picked from commit aa405b7da270595d349d0596ad31305a41d4b1c0)
